<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_Webwork.xml                   UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-25
  ============================================================================

  Puts the campaign's Webwork fauna roster onto RM_Webwork, adding to the
  vanilla Core-only roster that src/RimMandrake/Webwork/Defs/BiomeDefs/
  RM_Webwork_Biome.xml ships (Rat, Hare, Muffalo, Cobra, Megaspider — kept
  there so the Webwork mod is self-contained and works with nothing else
  loaded). The campaign wiring lives HERE, never in the Webwork mod itself.

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. §7 Q11 (owner, 2026-09-22): "RimMandrake should
  not name star wars ever." So RM_Webwork may not carry this cast, and at
  Phase B of design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md the RUT_Webwork def
  that currently carries it dies and RM_Webwork takes the tiles. Without this
  patch in place by then, the Webwork would lose its entire fauna cast on the
  live world. WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml / WildAnimals_Greentide.xml are the
  shape this copies.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH (AT AUTHORING, 2026-09-25): every defName and weight
  below is a verbatim copy of Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_Webwork.xml's own wildAnimals
  block (frozen 2026-09-25, the roster the world runs on today) — 4 rows,
  ALL Star Wars fauna (MEASURED, WEBWORK_RM_MOD_BUILD_1's own item file §3).
  This is the roster WEBWORK_FAUNA_ROSTER_1 is scoped to build the invented
  replacement/addition for and to execute its "3 ruled donor cuts" against —
  this file is NOT that item; it only wires today's live cast forward so nothing
  is lost between the freeze above and that item landing. Nothing here is
  rescaled. This file WILL diverge from the frozen twin going forward, same
  as WildAnimals_Greentide.xml already does — that is correct, not drift to
  reconcile.

  `RSW_JewelBeetle` and `RSW_Kreetle` are already our own RSW-tier ports
  (`mandrake.rsw.swbestiary` — the Kreetle repoint is
  DUPLICATE_CANON_DEFNAME_PAIRS_1's 2026-09-23 merge, already live in the
  frozen twin). `Wyyyschokk` and `Shyrack` are still the donor's own bare
  defNames (`mlie.starwarsanimalcollection`) — porting those, if ever ruled,
  is WEBWORK_FAUNA_ROSTER_1's call, not this file's.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match) — validate against the live def dump and the full
  active mod set before trusting a clean run as proof a row landed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)'s own bare defNames. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Webwork"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Webwork"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <Wyyyschokk>0.4</Wyyyschokk>
        <Shyrack>0.2</Shyrack>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Our own RSW-tier ports, from SWBestiary. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Webwork"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Webwork"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_JewelBeetle>0.3</RSW_JewelBeetle>
        <RSW_Kreetle>0.8</RSW_Kreetle>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
